---
description: Call recall before answering when context may already exist; call remember to save durable facts the user states.
alwaysApply: true
---

Before answering, when the request concerns people, projects, prior
decisions, or context the user expects you to already know, call the
`recall` tool first and use what it returns.

When the user states a durable fact worth keeping — a decision, a
preference, a status — call the `remember` tool to save it.

This is instructed recall: it depends on you actually following these
instructions on every turn. It is not automatic.
